(PRC-10b - `Change directory to` moves the working directory, and a
 bare relative name then resolves from it - done inside a forked child
 so the probe's own cwd never moves. The child first checks for a
 beacon directory by its bare name, so a failed chdir exits 3 before it
 creates anything in the wrong place. Shape of 'gen leaf process change
 directory in a child', kind 423 (process batch C, 2026-10-05).
 Ran, from the repo root, on the installed vox v0.4.15:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-10b.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   37
   the bare name landed in the new working directory
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
a text called harbour is "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_harbour".
Create a directory called harbour.
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_harbour/beacon".
a number called sailor is fork the process.
If sailor is 0 then, Change directory to harbour.
If sailor is 0 and "beacon" is not available then, Exit 3.
If sailor is 0 then, Create a directory called "skiff", Exit 37.
a number called 'sailor reaped' is reap child sailor.
Print the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256.
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_harbour/skiff" is available then, print "the bare name landed in the new working directory".
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_harbour/skiff".
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_harbour/beacon".
Remove the directory called harbour.
